// 01-LANGUAGE.md §5.3 (Q-62): a stack starts empty, unless the machine has the option
// "initial stack Z" (the Hopcroft–Motwani–Ullman convention).
pda P (initial stack Z) {
  start q0
  accept q1
  q0 -ε, Z → ε-> q1            // pops the initial Z
}
pda E {
  start q0
  accept q1
  q0 -ε, Z → ε-> q1            // the stack is empty, so this edge never fires
}
check P accepts ""
check E rejects ""
